Locators in PW - way to find and interact with webelements on page. 
Basic Syntax: 
page.locator('locator')

:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::Types of locators :::::::::::::::::

1. ********** CSS selector *********

page.locator('.submit-button')        // by class
page.locator('#username')             // by id
page.locator('button')                // by tag
page.locator('[type="submit"]')       // by attribute

2. ********** Text **********
page.locator('text=Login')            // exact text
page.locator('text=Log')              // partial text

3. ********** Xpath **********
page.locator('//button[@type="submit"]')

4. ********** getByRole **********
-> built on top of locator. It is more smarter & readable and recommended 
-> Allows locating elements by their ARIA role, ARIA attributes and accessible name.
-> 82 roles available in total

**ARAI - Set of special attributes added to the HTML tag to tell PW exactly what an element is(more info like button, radio,checkbox etc) and what it does regardless of tag. EX: arial-lable
ARAI attributs helps us to find the failed locators in fastest way because it holds the metadata 



