Key Feature 
Lazy initialization: A locator doesn't find the element immediately. It only searches when you perform an action.
This makes locator auto retrying, if element isnt there yet PW keeps trying until it appears or time out 

A locator is a reusable, lazy pointer to an element. getByRole, getByText etc. 
Are all just friendlier versions of the same concept — use them when you can, fall back to raw locator() when you need more control.

**************************************************************************

Othre locators [5]

5. getByText() - Non-interactive text like paragraphs, spans, or divs.	
page.getByText('Welcome to the Dashboard')

6. getByLabel()	- Form inputs that have a connected <label> tag.	
page.getByLabel('First Name')

7. getByPlaceholder()- Input fields that have placeholder text inside them.	
page.getByPlaceholder('Enter your email')

8. getByAltText() - Images (<img> tags) using their alt attribute.	
page.getByAltText('Company Logo')

9. getByTestId() - The "Emergency" option. Use when nothing else is stable.	
page.getByTestId('submit-button-id')



